```java
class Inventory {
    boolean reserve(String sku, int qty, String warehouseId) {
        int rows = stockLevelRepo.decrementAvailableIfSufficient(sku, warehouseId, qty);
        // UPDATE stock_levels SET reserved = reserved + ?
        // WHERE sku = ? AND warehouse_id = ?
        //   AND (on_hand - reserved) >= ?
        if (rows == 0) return false;

        reservationRepo.insert(sku, warehouseId, qty, ReservationStatus.ACTIVE);
        return true;
    }
}
```

The `WHERE (on_hand - reserved) >= ?` clause checks *available* stock, not on-hand — reserving never touches `onHand`, since nothing has physically left the warehouse yet. `onHand` only drops later, when the reservation is fulfilled (the item is actually picked and shipped).
